Description: refuse a pagination cursor that does not advance
Author: Azhou AI Hub
Forwarded: no

Both page walks loop while the reader hands back an endCursor. A GraphQL
connection that returned the same cursor twice, as a misbehaving proxy or a
retry against a stale page can, left the walk spinning: the watcher never
finished reading checks or review threads and never produced a verdict. A
repeated endCursor is now a retryable query error instead of another request.

